sfer outside the EU; sensitive data must be protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant).  4.3 Reliability and traceability of outputs. Any figure or factual statement produced by The solution must be grounded in, and traceable to, a source document; no ungrounded numeric output is acceptable. A complete audit trail and explainability are required, to support Cabinet Vauclair & Associés internal quality control and statutory-audit review.  4.4 Professional responsibility and independence. The solution is a non-decisional assistance tool; the chartered accountant or statutory auditor validates and signs. For statutory-audit (CAC) missions, The solution must respect the auditor’s independence and the separation of duties. The solution must not undermine Cabinet Vauclair & Associés anti-money-laundering obligations (LCB-FT). The titleholder must comply with the legal retention and archival obligations for accounting documents.  5. Technical constraints  5.1 Performance. Response times compatible with daily professional use are expected — as an indication, below 2 seconds for common queries — and The solution must sustain The solution performance during seasonal peak loads (closing periods, tax campaigns).  5.2 Availability. A high level of availability during business hours is required, with resilience to seasonal peak loads.  5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés production tools (accounting-production software, payroll software, document management / GED) and with the electronic-invoicing / dematerialisation environment. API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with the user directory (SSO).  6. Sovereignty constraints  Given the confidential financial nature of the data, hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is preferred, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers.  7. Budget constraints  The budget allocated to the project is, as an indication, €220,000 over 3 years. The annual operating cost must remain controlled. As Cabinet Vauclair & Associés is an SME, the titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service.  8. Environmental constraints  Cabinet Vauclair & Associés wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the solution and to rely, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure.  9. Deployment terms  the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on one office or one mission line, followed by progressive generalisation. Change-management support and training are expected. Ideally, a pilot should be operational before the next closing / tax campaign.  10. Evaluation criteria  Offers will be evaluated against: quality and relevance of the solution; reliability and traceability of outputs; confidentiality and security; respect of professional secrecy and of auditor independence; data sovereignty; quality of integration with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés production tools; total cost; quality of support; environmental considerations; capacity for innovation." ;
